From 69eb7b639abd000a08a8e8fba3b4cd0c757fd087 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BHARATH CHANDRA VADDARAM <bharath.vbcr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:05:26 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Track a resource reached through a field or a pointer by
 its access path

The written flag of a resource lived on the slot of the SSA value that loaded it, so
`h.w.Write(nil)` and `h.w.Close()` (two loads of one field) and `(*pw).Write` / `(*pw).Close`
never met on one slot, in a function and in a closure alike, and ERR005 missed them. resourceSlot
now keys such a resource on its root (a parameter, a captured variable, a local cell or any other
value) plus the dereferences and field selections applied to it, and a store to the same path
resets the slot to the stored value's written state, as a store to a captured variable already
did. A different field of the same holder, a replaced field and a read-only resource stay silent.

Four fixtures pinned the miss and flip in this commit, each with a ft-c7dd comment: advfv3b3c/a.go
P4b and P4b2, advfvctl3b3c/c.go C4 (the fixture itself calls it a true positive) and
advdeferend/adv.go's `(*T).done`, which is `generic` above it with a field in front.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
